  "question": {
    "text": "A survey shows that <math><mn>69</mn><mi>%</mi></math> students like mathematics, whereas <math><mn>75</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math> like chemistry. If <math><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math> students like both the subjects, then the maximum value of <math><mi>x</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "69",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, total students in survey be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math></p><p>If mathematics is represented by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> &amp; chemistry by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>, then&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br />Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>69</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math><br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>69</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>144</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>100</mn></math><br /><math><mn>75</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>144</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>100</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mn>44</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>69</mn></math></p>"
